30,2,1,talk,Servas,,It seems we have a surplus of theorists but a drought of technicians in certain specialized areas.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found that some costs are still subsidized, but others, like shipping, are becoming a burden.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Some facilities are totally full, while others are broken because the contracts lapsed!","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,Fieldwork is currently a gamble; nature has been quite unkind to several sites recently.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Interestingly, broad catalogs have a much longer shelf life than specific mechanism studies.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, does that mean we should avoid any project relying on external field sites?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, which facilities are the most congested? I worry about the budget for those.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"The glasshouses are packed, but the animal facilities seem to be in better shape now.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Servas. Biological risks in the wild are currently outweighing the rewards.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Toshio,,We should prioritize projects that provide a lasting resource for the community.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Servas,,I also noticed that some key analysts are simply not in the country right now.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Midori,,"That makes simulation-heavy work risky if the experts are gone, despite the free computing.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Kenji,,And the spectroscopy equipment is unreliable. We can't fund something that needs a broken machine.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems the safest bet is something indoor, stable, and perhaps data-driven.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Toshio,,I agree. Stability and utility should be our guiding stars.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
