55,3,1,talk,Servas,,"We have our candidates. A is a catalog, B is greenhouse work, C is spectroscopy and simulation, and D is amphibians.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Midori,,B is out; the glasshouses are booked solid and costs are rising.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Kenji,,C is out too! The spectroscopy suite is idle and the engineers are gone.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A is risky because of the field sites, and D relies on breeding colonies, which often overrun.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Toshio,,A is a catalog. My research shows those are the most enduring and useful awards.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Servas,,"But A needs field samples. @Benjamin, how bad is the situation at the sites?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Midori,,"If the repository turnaround is fast now, A's data would be available quickly.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried about the field sites, but A is better than a project that can't even start.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a risk, but D's breeding colonies are a known time-sink. A is more feasible.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Toshio,,A provides a permanent resource. It is the most rational choice.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I see that modeling posts are filling up, which helps A's data processing.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Midori,,And the computing is free. A is very cost-effective.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I vote for A. It's the most realistic given the facility logs.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. A is the least likely to be derailed by a broken machine or a full greenhouse.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I have already decided on A.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Servas,,I agree. The technical support for data is there. I vote A.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Midori,,I vote A as well.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
